AI Travel Itinerary Generator — Comprehensive Development Plan
1. PRD Analysis Summary
The AI Travel Itinerary Generator provides an intelligent way for users to generate detailed, day-by-day travel itineraries using AI (OpenAI API) and real-world data (Google Places API). The MVP targets frequent travelers, students, and professionals who want quick itinerary generation without manually searching multiple platforms.
Key MVP features include:
AI Itinerary Generation (destination + duration input)
Map Integration (Google Maps with daily pins)
Basic Authentication (JWT / Guest Mode)
Itinerary CRUD (Create, View, Edit, Delete)
Multilingual interface (English for MVP)

2. Technology Stack
Frontend
Framework: Next.js (v15.x)
UI Library: shadcn/ui
Language: TypeScript
Styling: Tailwind CSS
State Management: React Context API
API Communication: Axios / Fetch
Map Integration: Google Maps JavaScript API
Backend
Language: Python (v3.12.x)
Framework: FastAPI (v0.116.x)
Runtime: Uvicorn (ASGI server)
Authentication: JWT via python-jose
Data Validation: Pydantic v2.x
Environment Management: python-dotenv
Database
DBaaS: MongoDB Atlas (Free Tier)
ODM: Motor / PyMongo
Collections: users, itineraries, dayplans
External Integrations
OpenAI API: For itinerary content generation
Google Places API: For verifying points of interest & map pinning

3. Architecture Decision
Chosen Pattern: Modular Monolith
Justification:
Moderate complexity level (CRUD + API integrations)
Single developer team → faster development cycle
Easier local debugging, lighter DevOps footprint
Enables both frontend and backend to operate independently during development
Structure Overview: Frontend (Next.js) ↔ FastAPI Backend ↔ MongoDB Atlas
Both share common modular REST API structure in /api/v1/...

4. Domain-Driven Module Design
Frontend Modules
Auth Module: Register/Login screen + token management
Itinerary Module: Creation flow, daily plan display, itinerary list
Map Module: Google Maps rendering (per-day visualization)
Shared Components: NavBar, Footer, Theme selector
Backend Modules
User Module: Manages /auth routes, security, user CRUD
Itinerary Module: /itineraries CRUD endpoints
AI Integration Module: Connects OpenAI API for content generation
Map Module: Calls Google Places API for coordinates
Database Module: Connection setup and collection access
Shared Utilities: Token management, error handling, logging

